    "scenesThatPass": [
      "LADY JOAN: Down there. I live at Seal Court. My name's Bailey... Joan Bailey. I hope you don't mind. It's not too far...\nMAUD: We'll take you there.",
      "MAUD: That's what she must have seen.\nLADY JOAN: The east wing's never been used. I came here as a bride in 1929. No one's touched her room since then.\nLADY JOAN: We must find the scones. I'm afraid we don't have too many luxuries here. But one has to make an exception -- After tea, I think you should …",
      "LADY JOAN: I think we should get the bed made up, get some hot water bottles in it now. Don't you think, Dr. Bailey?\nMAUD: You're sure both of us can stay. This isn't an imposition --\nLADY JOAN: Nonsense --",
      "MAUD: No. I'll go...\nLADY JOAN: I hope you haven't had a tiff, or something.",
      "MAUD: Just this one...\nMAUD: '... My dear friend, how shall I answer? Your inspiration means so much to me. Yet I feel I cannot continue our correspondence. Blanche and …\nCHRISTABEL: '... You will say you are no threat to that. I know the threat is there. Perhaps it would be better if we ceased to correspond...'"
    ]
